# Test Fixtures for trap_census.py --texts

This directory contains hand-built test fixtures for the `--texts` flag of `trap_census.py`.

## Fixtures

- `fixture_green_simple.bp` — A minimal Bebop source file using the str-literal form
  (`diag_str`) for diagnostic texts. This matches the post-L30 format (after step 1 lands).

- `fixture_green_simple.bin` — A BYTE FIXTURE (not a compiled binary artifact). Contains
  the raw byte strings of the texts used in the corresponding `.bp` file, allowing the
  check to verify texts are present in the binary. Hand-built with NUL padding.

- `fixture_red_perturbed.bin` — A BYTE FIXTURE with one text string missing from
  `fixture_green_simple.bin`, used to verify the check detects disagreement and reports
  which code is missing.

These `.bin` files are NOT compiled artifacts from the Bebop compiler. They are plain
byte containers used to test the text-search logic in isolation from compilation.
